{
 "about": "Front HI0: the hi glossary (plan analysis/front-plans/front-i18n-hi.md §5) that src/i18n/hi/hi.test.ts enforces through the SC4 lint framework (src/i18n/lint/, profile hi) on every Hindi string. Seeded from the French glossary: the same English patterns and interface names, re-targeted to Hindi from the English by Sonnet batches and corrected by the HI0 implementer. A term applies when its English pattern matches the English source: the Hindi must then match the `hi` stem or pattern (case-insensitive, Unicode). Names are fixed interface names (an exact name applies only to a whole string); the Hindi must contain the `hi` text. Forbidden are the term forms this glossary rejects (टेलीस्कोप, चयन करें, मंदाकिनी and गैलेक्सी for galaxy, लाल विचलन for redshift, हबल स्थिरांक, तरंगदैर्ध्य, अनधिकृत and अनौपचारिक for unofficial, प्लीएडीज़); the language-wide rules (the danda and other typography, the आप register and the तुम forms it rejects, nukta loanwords, spelling, formal words, claims that a translation is CLEA's or official) live in the hi profile of src/i18n/lint/profiles.ts. Sources: Hindi Wikipedia (आकाशगंगा in हबल का नियम for galaxies, अभिरक्त विस्थापन, हबल नियतांक, कृत्तिका तारागुच्छ, read 2026-11-19), NCERT usage and the Microsoft Hindi style guide; no IAU OAE or current CSTT astronomy list was available, so terms are usage, not a standard. VIREO's names follow the plan's decided forms (Save सहेजें, Record दर्ज करें, Find ढूँढें, Search खोजें, Show दिखाएँ, Display प्रदर्शन, Slew घुमाएँ, Init/Go तैयार करें/शुरू करें, Scan क्रम से देखें, Clear साफ़ करें, Reset रीसेट करें, Hot List वस्तु सूची, lab प्रयोग). Rows for areas still in English wait for their sub-front (HI1–HI6) to be checked against their screens.",
